{
  "title": "Wat heb je gisteren gemaakt?",
  "goal": "Talk about yesterday with hebben and a regular past participle.",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 1
      },
      "content": "Wat heb je gisteren gemaakt?",
      "id": "a90bc6bc-58ed-4b98-a275-7c564b187a14"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "It is Monday 4 January 2027. Sofia is back in Utrecht and sees Noor. They talk about the holidays and Sunday. In this lesson you will use hebben + a past participle to talk about completed activities. Verbs are blue, subjects green, time expressions orange and the new participle is bold.",
      "id": "1dd832ca-3cf0-4061-8db4-ac74e867a46d"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "content": "Story: back in Utrecht",
      "id": "513029a0-fdbb-4c34-89b4-7ba28b2c3b2d"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "props": {
        "turns": [
          {
            "speaker": "Noor",
            "text": "Hoi Sofia! Fijn dat je terug bent!"
          },
          {
            "speaker": "Sofia",
            "text": "Hoi Noor! Ik ben blij dat ik thuis ben."
          },
          {
            "speaker": "Noor",
            "text": "Wat heb je gisteren gemaakt?"
          },
          {
            "speaker": "Sofia",
            "text": "Ik heb thee gemaakt en mijn kamer opgeruimd."
          },
          {
            "speaker": "Noor",
            "text": "En heb je ook gekookt?"
          },
          {
            "speaker": "Sofia",
            "text": "Nee, ik heb niet gekookt. Ik heb thee gemaakt."
          },
          {
            "speaker": "Noor",
            "text": "En heb je thee gemaakt?"
          },
          {
            "speaker": "Sofia",
            "text": "Ja, en ik heb mijn moeder gebeld."
          }
        ]
      },
      "id": "9b9c890b-079a-4ff2-b65c-3e550fb99076"
    },
    {
      "type": "vocabulary",
      "props": {
        "data": {
          "words": [
            {
              "term": "Heb je …?",
              "meaning": "Have you …?; a question with hebben",
              "example": "Heb je ook gekookt?",
              "id": "8c868377-6a27-479d-adb2-ab12d98b0930"
            },
            {
              "term": "Wat heb je …?",
              "meaning": "What did you …?; asks about a completed activity",
              "example": "Wat heb je gisteren gemaakt?",
              "id": "a36f64fe-83c2-4d7d-a26f-e1ba70efea25"
            },
            {
              "term": "gisteren",
              "meaning": "yesterday",
              "example": "Ik heb gisteren gewerkt.",
              "id": "16509e73-1d99-42cb-9db9-18abd045e35e"
            },
            {
              "term": "maken",
              "meaning": "to make",
              "forms": "maakt · maakte · gemaakt",
              "example": "Ik heb thee gemaakt.",
              "id": "6606e1c5-33bd-4fd5-b5cb-c49c7b6ecd66",
              "note": "The infinitive is known from an earlier lesson; this lesson introduces its past participle."
            },
            {
              "term": "koken",
              "meaning": "to cook",
              "forms": "kookt · kookte · gekookt",
              "example": "Heb je gisteren gekookt?",
              "id": "4eccdd5a-d849-4567-b3dc-6709718adf7e",
              "note": "The infinitive is known from an earlier lesson; this lesson introduces its past participle."
            },
            {
              "term": "bellen",
              "meaning": "to call",
              "forms": "belt · belde · gebeld",
              "example": "Noor heeft Sofia gebeld.",
              "id": "c2d7f002-b590-4c0d-bcce-a9d69670859a",
              "note": "The infinitive is known from an earlier lesson; this lesson introduces its past participle."
            },
            {
              "term": "Ik heb …",
              "meaning": "I have …; a sentence starter for a completed activity",
              "example": "Ik heb gisteren gewerkt.",
              "id": "897dfdbe-4be6-4c44-a88b-85329364245d"
            },
            {
              "term": "opruimen",
              "meaning": "to tidy up",
              "forms": "ruimt op · ruimde op · opgeruimd",
              "note": "The infinitive is known from an earlier lesson; this lesson introduces its past participle.",
              "example": "Ik heb mijn kamer opgeruimd.",
              "id": "744fb812-c244-466c-b390-2bd7b3d8ae4c"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "id": "cdff3e59-836f-41c3-9443-67ff993c74cb"
    },
    {
      "type": "divider",
      "id": "0a4cc446-e495-47dd-ad9c-8c8ab6ec6907"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "content": "The perfect: hebben + past participle",
      "id": "c5daa47b-7062-487c-9edf-4c9e434e9db2"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "For a completed activity, use the present form of hebben and put the past participle at the end. The helper verb changes; the participle usually starts with ge-.",
      "id": "65c5fada-15b9-4402-a0a2-0c3ae37b0c5d"
    },
    {
      "type": "callout",
      "props": {
        "variant": "grammar",
        "icon": "book-open"
      },
      "content": "Subject + hebben + other words + past participle: Ik heb gisteren gewerkt. In a yes/no question, hebben comes first: Heb je gewerkt?",
      "id": "f66281d1-e8e3-41b8-8785-6081cc944da0"
    },
    {
      "type": "vocabulary",
      "props": {
        "data": {
          "words": [
            {
              "term": "het voltooid deelwoord",
              "meaning": "the past participle",
              "example": "Gewerkt is het voltooid deelwoord van werken.",
              "id": "648744d0-56c3-4418-9df1-769af1948c9b"
            },
            {
              "term": "het hulpwerkwoord",
              "meaning": "the auxiliary verb",
              "example": "Hebben is het hulpwerkwoord in Ik heb gewerkt.",
              "id": "86a3c50c-ccb1-44c1-ae77-29ecd88524ed"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "id": "85d82328-11e1-43db-8350-b6082dd8b59f"
    },
    {
      "type": "example",
      "props": {
        "translation": "I worked yesterday.",
        "note": "The present form heb is the helper; gewerkt is the past participle."
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "text": "Ik",
          "styles": {
            "textColor": "green"
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " heb",
          "styles": {
            "textColor": "blue"
          }
        },
        " gisteren ",
        {
          "text": "gewerkt",
          "styles": {
            "bold": true,
            "backgroundColor": "yellow"
          }
        },
        "."
      ],
      "id": "1219eef6-edea-4d93-9295-e2d2860856d1"
    },
    {
      "type": "vocabulary",
      "props": {
        "data": {
          "words": [
            {
              "term": "werken",
              "meaning": "to work",
              "forms": "werkt · werkte · gewerkt",
              "example": "Ik heb gisteren gewerkt.",
              "id": "d27eb976-f050-4bff-b43d-6f56c8c2fb99",
              "note": "The infinitive is known from an earlier lesson; this lesson introduces its past participle."
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "id": "614de25d-f15b-400c-8f54-0fe2cbc5f61c"
    },
    {
      "type": "example",
      "props": {
        "translation": "Noor called Sofia.",
        "note": "Noor is the subject; heeft is the form of hebben for she."
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "text": "Noor",
          "styles": {
            "textColor": "green"
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " heeft",
          "styles": {
            "textColor": "blue"
          }
        },
        " Sofia ",
        {
          "text": "gebeld",
          "styles": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        "."
      ],
      "id": "df091192-e833-4dbc-984c-a20f82fead2c"
    },
    {
      "type": "example",
      "props": {
        "translation": "Did you cook yesterday?",
        "note": "In a yes/no question, heb comes before the subject."
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "text": "Heb",
          "styles": {
            "textColor": "blue"
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " je",
          "styles": {
            "textColor": "green"
          }
        },
        " gisteren ",
        {
          "text": "gekookt",
          "styles": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        "?"
      ],
      "id": "38d908d1-b662-4635-8b6e-482a8ff9ebe7"
    },
    {
      "type": "example",
      "props": {
        "translation": "We made tea at home.",
        "note": "Recycles thuis and thee from earlier lessons."
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "text": "We",
          "styles": {
            "textColor": "green"
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " hebben",
          "styles": {
            "textColor": "blue"
          }
        },
        " thuis thee ",
        {
          "text": "gemaakt",
          "styles": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        "."
      ],
      "id": "7f4544e8-e69c-4a01-80f2-086eced22b8c"
    },
    {
      "type": "example",
      "props": {
        "translation": "Sofia learned Dutch.",
        "note": "The participle geleerd ends in -d because the stem ends in r."
      },
      "content": [
        "Sofia heeft Nederlands ",
        {
          "text": "geleerd",
          "styles": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        "."
      ],
      "id": "b4490965-ba39-4d75-bfc2-17b5d40cf473"
    },
    {
      "type": "vocabulary",
      "props": {
        "data": {
          "words": [
            {
              "term": "leren",
              "meaning": "to learn",
              "forms": "leert · leerde · geleerd",
              "example": "Ik heb Nederlands geleerd.",
              "id": "5a775ce3-a10b-4acf-a0e8-f5d2892cc3cc",
              "note": "The infinitive is known from an earlier lesson; this lesson introduces its past participle."
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "id": "31e2320a-cabc-4cbe-8604-9b5f23e042a3"
    },
    {
      "type": "example",
      "props": {
        "translation": "Did you call your mother?",
        "note": "Heb comes first in the yes/no question; the object comes before gebeld."
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "text": "Heb",
          "styles": {
            "textColor": "blue"
          }
        },
        " je je moeder ",
        {
          "text": "gebeld",
          "styles": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        "?"
      ],
      "id": "815a9f1f-0044-44a0-ad94-6a869d5bfdb8"
    },
    {
      "type": "example",
      "props": {
        "translation": "Daan worked yesterday.",
        "note": "The time expression comes before the participle."
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "text": "Daan",
          "styles": {
            "textColor": "green"
          }
        },
        " heeft gisteren ",
        {
          "text": "gewerkt",
          "styles": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        "."
      ],
      "id": "679b995f-e026-40fa-927e-f091196db447"
    },
    {
      "type": "example",
      "props": {
        "translation": "Did you learn Dutch?",
        "note": "The helper verb comes first; geleerd is at the end."
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "text": "Heb",
          "styles": {
            "textColor": "blue"
          }
        },
        " je Nederlands ",
        {
          "text": "geleerd",
          "styles": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        "?"
      ],
      "id": "2b3758c7-5ad8-4ecb-8961-ed9280246e0d"
    },
