    {
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 3
      },
      "content": "How do you choose -t or -d?",
      "id": "bcf4e067-b90d-4db0-9c4b-ec599382dd01"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Take the verb stem (de stam). Its final sound (de eindklank) decides the ending. If it is in 't kofschip (t, k, f, s, ch, p), the participle ends in -t. Otherwise it ends in -d. Keep the spelling of the stem: maken becomes gemaakt; wonen becomes gewoond.",
      "id": "8dcac270-c52c-4ea9-9ed0-6ab69361d466"
    },
    {
      "type": "vocabulary",
      "props": {
        "data": {
          "words": [
            {
              "term": "de stam",
              "meaning": "the verb stem",
              "example": "De stam van werken is werk.",
              "id": "c1d827ce-b7bf-4178-a962-eea8e5ff0ae0"
            },
            {
              "term": "de eindklank",
              "meaning": "the final sound",
              "example": "De eindklank van werk is k.",
              "id": "f15a32fe-83d0-4b82-af4c-aa5a4ed38352"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "id": "87df8939-4018-4f50-8731-1abef7b8e0c0"
    },
    {
      "type": "callout",
      "props": {
        "variant": "pronunciation",
        "icon": "volume-2"
      },
      "content": "The final -t or -d is often quiet in everyday speech, but it stays in the spelling. Say gewerkt with a clear final t and gewoond with a final d.",
      "id": "8be0adba-bf88-4b3b-9dd2-4695ef594caf"
    },
    {
      "type": "example",
      "props": {
        "translation": "I cleaned my room.",
        "note": "The final stem sound of opruim is m, so the participle ends in -d."
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "text": "Ik",
          "styles": {
            "textColor": "green"
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " heb",
          "styles": {
            "textColor": "blue"
          }
        },
        " mijn kamer ",
        {
          "text": "opgeruimd",
          "styles": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        "."
      ],
      "id": "86cf0853-779a-4703-855c-7f66bc53ce38"
    },
    {
      "type": "example",
      "props": {
        "translation": "We studied Dutch.",
        "note": "The final stem sound of leer is r, so the participle ends in -d."
      },
      "content": [
        "We hebben Nederlands ",
        {
          "text": "geleerd",
          "styles": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        "."
      ],
      "id": "e5ee9805-714a-462d-b787-554f3debb328"
    },
    {
      "type": "callout",
      "props": {
        "variant": "important",
        "icon": "star"
      },
      "content": "The participle goes at the end: Ik heb mijn kamer gisteren opgeruimd. Put other sentence parts before it.",
      "id": "41991fd2-145d-47c4-a795-cce266cd39b5"
    },
    {
      "type": "callout",
      "props": {
        "variant": "warning",
        "icon": "triangle-alert"
      },
      "content": [
        "Wrong: ",
        {
          "text": "Ik heb gewerkt gisteren.",
          "styles": {
            "italic": true,
            "backgroundColor": "gray"
          }
        },
        " Correct: Ik heb gisteren gewerkt."
      ],
      "id": "47a11c66-ad50-4d08-ab5d-241912d81478"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 3
      },
      "content": "A Christmas catch-up",
      "id": "1bfc3b80-e8c3-4fcc-a967-706b7cbf69cd"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Sofia and Noor also remember Christmas. These are familiar events, told now with a new verb form.",
      "id": "cf0fcf19-f774-478a-bac5-c6f64d4a5878"
    },
    {
      "type": "example",
      "props": {
        "translation": "At Christmas, I cooked with my mother.",
        "note": "Met kerst is a time expression. In a statement, the finite verb comes before the subject after a fronted time expression."
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "text": "Met kerst",
          "styles": {
            "textColor": "orange"
          }
        },
        " heb ik met mijn moeder gekookt."
      ],
      "id": "d0a39613-c7c3-4aff-bd3d-78ee25269cd0"
    },
    {
      "type": "vocabulary",
      "props": {
        "data": {
          "words": [
            {
              "term": "met kerst",
              "meaning": "at Christmas",
              "example": "Met kerst heb ik gewerkt.",
              "id": "243e8683-48a7-4437-8be7-ab9a431677f8"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "id": "5bcbef04-ca32-4a4b-a005-d7f2f5d7b550"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "props": {
        "turns": [
          {
            "speaker": "Noor",
            "text": "Heb je met kerst gekookt?"
          },
          {
            "speaker": "Sofia",
            "text": "Ja, ik heb met mijn moeder gekookt."
          },
          {
            "speaker": "Noor",
            "text": "Heb je ook gekookt?"
          },
          {
            "speaker": "Sofia",
            "text": "Nee, ik heb niet gekookt. Ik heb thee gemaakt."
          },
          {
            "speaker": "Noor",
            "text": "Heb je veel Nederlands geleerd?"
          },
          {
            "speaker": "Sofia",
            "text": "Ja, ik heb veel Nederlands geleerd."
          },
          {
            "speaker": "Noor",
            "text": "Heb je Nederlands geleerd?"
          },
          {
            "speaker": "Sofia",
            "text": "Ja, ik heb Nederlands geleerd."
          }
        ]
      },
      "id": "df05b8f6-dc0e-4dbb-8892-2b3cb0cea5f1"
    },
    {
      "type": "bulletListItem",
      "content": "Regular participles usually begin with ge-.",
      "id": "738e76be-ea53-4d1b-a956-e5e3a9c58bd8"
    },
    {
      "type": "bulletListItem",
      "content": "The stem's final sound decides -t or -d.",
      "children": [
        {
          "type": "bulletListItem",
          "content": "'t kofschip sound: -t (gewerkt, gekookt).",
          "id": "5667c000-3a0e-4908-b6c3-db7c3c3e48fd"
        },
        {
          "type": "bulletListItem",
          "content": "Other sounds: -d (gebeld, geleerd).",
          "id": "7fbbde80-d597-4e73-a543-e1df1ac1e624"
        }
      ],
      "id": "d16c9953-8126-4721-b84a-12cd21e80946"
    },
    {
      "type": "bulletListItem",
      "content": "A separable verb puts ge between prefix and verb: opruimen → opgeruimd.",
      "id": "2ec988e1-9c06-42bf-b4a0-1fdc14de38b6"
    },
    {
      "type": "divider",
      "id": "a4a371c7-f626-4aba-bc51-f3fffe6125f5"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "content": "Practice",
      "id": "46c47502-4cbd-41ff-8544-7be3dfdcb23e"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 3
      },
      "content": "Complete the sentence",
      "id": "300de1bc-b483-4295-8530-0e93826f7a69"
    },
    {
      "type": "practice",
      "props": {
        "data": {
          "instruction": "Fill in the present form of hebben and the past participle.",
          "items": [
            {
              "prompt": "Ik … gisteren … . (werken)",
              "authorsVersion": [
                "heb",
                "gewerkt"
              ],
              "note": "Ik takes heb; werken has -t after k."
            },
            {
              "prompt": "Noor … thee … . (maken)",
              "authorsVersion": [
                "heeft",
                "gemaakt"
              ],
              "note": "Noor takes heeft; the stem spelling maak stays visible."
            },
            {
              "prompt": "Wij … thuis … . (koken)",
              "authorsVersion": [
                "hebben",
                "gekookt"
              ],
              "note": "The stem ends in k, so use -t."
            },
            {
              "prompt": "Sofia … Nederlands … . (leren)",
              "authorsVersion": [
                "heeft",
                "geleerd"
              ],
              "note": "The stem ends in r, so use -d."
            },
            {
              "prompt": "Daan … Noor … . (bellen)",
              "authorsVersion": [
                "heeft",
                "gebeld"
              ],
              "note": "The stem ends in l, so use -d."
            },
            {
              "prompt": "Jullie … gisteren … . (wonen)",
              "authorsVersion": [
                "hebben",
                "gewoond"
              ],
              "note": "The plural helper is hebben; the stem ends in n, so use -d."
            },
            {
              "prompt": "Ik … mijn kamer … . (opruimen)",
              "authorsVersion": [
                "heb",
                "opgeruimd"
              ],
              "note": "Separable prefix op surrounds ge in the participle."
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "id": "305cdcb5-3dc0-4b2f-914c-4263e323dc37"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 3
      },
      "content": "Choose the ending",
      "id": "2e0a4485-1189-405f-945d-18059433ab07"
    },
    {
      "type": "practice",
      "props": {
        "data": {
          "instruction": "Complete each participle with -t or -d.",
          "items": [
            {
              "prompt": "gewerk…",
              "authorsVersion": [
                "gewerkt"
              ],
              "note": "The stem ends in k, a 't kofschip sound."
            },
            {
              "prompt": "gewoon…",
              "authorsVersion": [
                "gewoond"
              ],
              "note": "The stem ends in n, so use d."
            },
            {
              "prompt": "gemaak…",
              "authorsVersion": [
                "gemaakt"
              ],
              "note": "The stem ends in k, so use t."
            },
            {
              "prompt": "gebel…",
              "authorsVersion": [
                "gebeld"
              ],
              "note": "The stem ends in l, so use d."
            },
            {
              "prompt": "gekook…",
              "authorsVersion": [
                "gekookt"
              ],
              "note": "The stem ends in k, so use t."
            },
            {
              "prompt": "geleer…",
              "authorsVersion": [
                "geleerd"
              ],
              "note": "The stem ends in r, so use d."
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "id": "525d4a0e-5fee-4183-85f0-26e99da1f769"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 3
      },
      "content": "Complete the dialogue",
      "id": "98e026c8-63c5-4902-aa85-bdb9b24c7d9f"
    },
    {
      "type": "practice",
      "props": {
        "data": {
          "instruction": "Fill in the missing helper or participle.",
          "items": [
            {
              "prompt": "Noor: Wat … je gisteren …? (maken) / Sofia: Ik … thee … .",
              "authorsVersion": [
                "heb",
                "gemaakt",
                "heb",
                "gemaakt"
              ],
              "note": "Heb comes first in the question; heb je in the answer."
            },
            {
              "prompt": "Sofia: … Noor ook …? (koken) / Noor: Ja, ik … pasta … .",
              "authorsVersion": [
                "Heeft",
                "gekookt",
                "heb",
                "gekookt"
              ],
              "note": "Noor is she, so the question starts with Heeft."
            },
            {
              "prompt": "Daan: … jullie thuis …? (werken) / Sofia: Ja, we … thuis … .",
              "authorsVersion": [
                "Hebben",
                "gewerkt",
                "hebben",
                "gewerkt"
              ],
              "note": "Plural subject jullie/we takes hebben."
            },
            {
              "prompt": "Noor: … je de kamer …? (opruimen) / Sofia: Ja, ik … hem … .",
              "authorsVersion": [
                "Heb",
                "opgeruimd",
                "heb",
                "opgeruimd"
              ],
              "note": "Keep the separable prefix around ge. hem refers to the room here."
            },
            {
              "prompt": "Sofia: … je Nederlands …? (leren) / Noor: Ja, ik … veel … .",
              "authorsVersion": [
                "Heb",
                "geleerd",
                "heb",
                "geleerd"
              ],
              "note": "The participle goes at the end."
            },
            {
              "prompt": "Noor: … je moeder …? (bellen) / Sofia: Ja, ik … haar … .",
              "authorsVersion": [
                "Heb",
                "gebeld",
                "heb",
                "gebeld"
              ],
              "note": "The direct object comes before the participle."
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "id": "25967393-60b0-42f0-ac5c-7dcabda261ad"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 3
      },
      "content": "Put the participle last",
      "id": "bd1dadbc-9036-454f-a4ad-9d19fb754036"
    },
    {
      "type": "practice",
      "props": {
        "data": {
          "instruction": "Put the chunks in order. Write the full sentence.",
          "items": [
            {
              "prompt": "gisteren / ik / heb / gewerkt",
              "authorsVersion": [
                "Ik heb gisteren gewerkt."
              ],
              "note": "The participle closes the sentence."
            },
            {
              "prompt": "heeft / Sofia / thee / gemaakt",
              "authorsVersion": [
                "Sofia heeft thee gemaakt."
              ],
              "note": "The object comes before the participle."
            },
            {
              "prompt": "gisteren / hebben / we / gekookt / samen",
              "authorsVersion": [
                "We hebben gisteren samen gekookt."
              ],
              "note": "The time and manner phrase come before the participle."
            },
            {
              "prompt": "heb / opgeruimd / ik / mijn kamer",
              "authorsVersion": [
                "Ik heb mijn kamer opgeruimd."
              ],
              "note": "The separable participle stays together at the end."
            },
            {
              "prompt": "geleerd / Nederlands / heeft / Noor",
              "authorsVersion": [
                "Noor heeft Nederlands geleerd."
              ],
              "note": "The helper follows the subject; the participle is last."
            },
            {
              "prompt": "gebeld / heb / mijn moeder / ik",
              "authorsVersion": [
                "Ik heb mijn moeder gebeld."
              ],
              "note": "Keep the object before the participle."
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "id": "b21a17bd-e083-440a-8a97-c1e435c879a8"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 3
      },
      "content": "Change present to perfect",
      "id": "e23c2ef1-3395-4760-905e-8deed028505b"
    },
    {
      "type": "practice",
      "props": {
        "data": {
          "instruction": "Rewrite each sentence with hebben + a past participle.",
          "items": [
            {
              "prompt": "Ik werk thuis.",
              "authorsVersion": [
                "Ik heb thuis gewerkt."
              ],
              "note": "Add heb and put gewerkt at the end."
            },
            {
              "prompt": "Noor maakt thee.",
              "authorsVersion": [
                "Noor heeft thee gemaakt."
              ],
              "note": "Noor takes heeft."
            },
            {
              "prompt": "Wij koken samen.",
              "authorsVersion": [
                "Wij hebben samen gekookt."
              ],
              "note": "Plural subject takes hebben."
            },
            {
              "prompt": "Sofia ruimt haar kamer op.",
              "authorsVersion": [
                "Sofia heeft haar kamer opgeruimd."
              ],
              "note": "Separable op goes around ge in the participle."
            },
            {
              "prompt": "Daan belt Lotte.",
              "authorsVersion": [
                "Daan heeft Lotte gebeld."
              ],
              "note": "The object comes before the participle."
            },
            {
              "prompt": "Ik leer Nederlands.",
              "authorsVersion": [
                "Ik heb Nederlands geleerd."
              ],
              "note": "The stem ends in r, so geleerd ends in d."
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "id": "8b84bf3a-f51c-4876-a25c-21786a43b822"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 3
      },
      "content": "Translate into Dutch",
      "id": "9f130f41-83db-47d7-82bd-84f25f1d6dd2"
    },
    {
      "type": "practice",
      "props": {
        "data": {
          "instruction": "Translate into natural Dutch.",
          "items": [
            {
              "prompt": "I worked yesterday.",
              "authorsVersion": [
                "Ik heb gisteren gewerkt."
              ]
            },
            {
              "prompt": "Noor made tea.",
              "authorsVersion": [
                "Noor heeft thee gemaakt."
              ],
              "note": "The participle goes at the end."
            },
            {
              "prompt": "Did you cook yesterday?",
              "authorsVersion": [
                "Heb je gisteren gekookt?"
              ],
              "note": "Heb comes before je in a yes/no question."
            },
            {
              "prompt": "We tidied the room.",
              "authorsVersion": [
                "We hebben de kamer opgeruimd."
              ],
              "note": "Use opgeruimd as one participle."
            },
            {
              "prompt": "I called my mother.",
              "authorsVersion": [
                "Ik heb mijn moeder gebeld."
              ]
            },
            {
              "prompt": "At Christmas, we studied Dutch.",
              "authorsVersion": [
                "Met kerst hebben we Nederlands geleerd."
              ],
              "note": "Also fine: We hebben met kerst Nederlands geleerd."
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "id": "8804a93c-744d-49fd-af2c-ccdd57b05014"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 3
      },
      "content": "Translate into English",
      "id": "63b7d0f6-089d-4cca-b6ef-d12108b782f1"
    },
    {
      "type": "practice",
      "props": {
        "data": {
          "instruction": "Translate into natural English.",
          "items": [
            {
              "prompt": "Ik heb gisteren gewerkt.",
              "authorsVersion": [
                "I worked yesterday."
              ]
            },
            {
              "prompt": "Heb je thee gemaakt?",
              "authorsVersion": [
                "Did you make tea?"
              ],
              "note": "Dutch uses hebben + participle; natural English uses the simple past."
            },
            {
              "prompt": "Noor heeft Sofia gebeld.",
              "authorsVersion": [
                "Noor called Sofia."
              ]
            },
            {
              "prompt": "We hebben samen gekookt.",
              "authorsVersion": [
                "We cooked together."
              ]
            },
            {
              "prompt": "Ik heb mijn kamer opgeruimd.",
              "authorsVersion": [
                "I tidied my room."
              ]
            },
            {
              "prompt": "Met kerst heeft Daan thuis gewerkt.",
              "authorsVersion": [
                "At Christmas, Daan worked from home."
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "id": "7b882b4e-34b0-4c15-813c-f1467bfc9757"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "content": "Reading: Sunday at home",
      "id": "2dca9bb2-16f5-4bf5-8f08-6e2c1059f8fb"
    },
    {
      "type": "practice",
      "props": {
        "data": {
          "instruction": "Read Sofia's note and answer in Dutch.",
          "passage": {
            "title": "Een bericht van Sofia",
            "content": "Maandag 4 januari\nGisteren heb ik thee gemaakt en mijn kamer opgeruimd. Daarna heb ik mijn moeder gebeld. Vandaag zie ik Noor. Met kerst heb ik met mijn moeder gekookt en Nederlands geleerd."
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "prompt": "Welke dag is het in het verhaal?",
              "authorsVersion": [
                "Maandag 4 januari."
              ]
            },
            {
              "prompt": "Wat heeft Sofia gemaakt?",
              "authorsVersion": [
                "Thee."
              ]
            },
            {
              "prompt": "Wat heeft Sofia met kerst geleerd?",
              "authorsVersion": [
                "Nederlands."
              ]
            },
            {
              "prompt": "Wie heeft thee gemaakt?",
              "authorsVersion": [
                "Sofia."
              ],
              "note": "The note is written by Sofia."
            },
            {
              "prompt": "Wat heeft Sofia gisteren opgeruimd?",
              "authorsVersion": [
                "Haar kamer."
              ],
              "note": "The answer is in the first sentence."
            },
            {
              "prompt": "Met wie heeft Sofia met kerst gekookt?",
              "authorsVersion": [
                "Met haar moeder."
              ],
              "note": "Met wie asks who she cooked with."
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "id": "57309903-1cdd-45e7-ac54-cd2376856895"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "content": "Your turn",
      "id": "1f742b7d-11ee-4e64-8d7f-eba0dca4ec0a"
    },
    {
      "type": "practice",
      "props": {
        "data": {
          "instruction": "Write three short sentences about yesterday or another recent day. Use at least two participles and a time expression.",
          "items": [
            {
              "prompt": "Write three short sentences about a recent day.",
              "authorsVersion": [
                "Gisteren heb ik thuis gewerkt. Ik heb thee gemaakt en mijn kamer opgeruimd."
              ],
              "note": "Answers will vary. Keep hebben after the subject and put each participle at the end."
            }
          ]
        }
